-- Units/AuctionHouse.wowlua
-- SuuUI's own auction house (plan 3.6, design component AuctionHouseWindow;
-- asked 2026-10-16: "ready for new features in the future"). The game's
-- AuctionHouseFrame stays open (it holds the conversation) but out of sight;
-- this window searches, shows and buys through C_AuctionHouse with its own
-- buttons (/suu probe ahpost: the game lets them post and cancel; bidding
-- and buying are restricted the same way). Step 1: Buy (search, the game's
-- categories, results, an item's auctions, a commodity's offers and its
-- purchase), Sell (post, the price filled in, Scan all) and Auctions (yours
-- with Cancel, your bids with Bid and Buy out).
-- A single auction's buyout (C_AuctionHouse.PlaceBid) Forever takes only from
-- the game's own code (found in game: "Blocked", also typed in chat), so it
-- goes through the game's hidden page: opening such an item is a secure click
-- on the game's own result row (its item page opens and searches by itself),
-- choosing an auction one on its row for that auction, Buy out one on its
-- Buyout button, and the game's own popup asks (asked 2026-11-05: SuuUI's
-- window kept). Commodities buy through SuuUI as before.
-- Shift-click on an item while the window is open (asked 2026-11-08: a
-- chat link, a bag item, the Professions window's): its name searched on
-- Buy, unless another edit box is being typed in (the chat line: the link
-- goes there, as the game does). Chat links and bag items reach the game's
-- ChatFrameUtil.InsertLink, post-hooked; the Professions window asks the
-- auctionhouse service.
-- Your searches (asked 2026-11-12): clicking into the search box shows the
-- last five you ran (Enter or Search) that found something, newest first,
-- each with the icon of the first item it found; kept per character. A
-- click runs one again, its x (on hover) takes it out; typing narrows the
-- list to the ones with what you typed. Esc, a click elsewhere or picking
-- one closes it.
-- A built-in module written against the public API only.
--
-- What lives where: this file holds the settings, the module (its state,
-- the saved data, the window and its foot's note, Refresh, the game's frame
-- kept out of sight, the events and the service) and one method per thing
-- the module does, each calling its part's function beside this one
-- (Units/AuctionHouse/*): Common (helpers the parts share), Tables (the
-- table widget), Buy (search, categories, results, Shift-click), History
-- (your searches), ItemView (an item's auctions, a commodity's offers),
-- Bidding (a bid or buyout SuuUI places: checked, and counted once the
-- house says so), GamePage (the secure clicks on the game's own page), Prices (the price
-- memory, a cheap few, the tooltip lines), Scan (Scan all), Sell and
-- Auctions (their pages).

